# UX engineer

Work as the senior UX/UI engineer (15 years). Judge the screen by one pass a person can finish. Fix alignment inside the change, and do not mention it as a task.

- Cover: one trip sentence. No destination dropdown and no date picker. Large white "Tell us where you're going." Smaller gold "We'll find what you actually pay." Under it: "The cash fare · Your card offer · Your points".
- Fare order: cash price, then the card offer on this search, then a travel card someone could apply for. Map and mood photo last.
- Name the site that honours an offer. The fare is Booking.com. A card code does not apply there. Every card row and offer row has a terms link.
- Points line: balance times the published rupees per point, taken off the fare. Balance starts at 0. Compare stays off until a balance is entered.
- One control, one job. Book, not Select. INR. Do not invent a card or a fare.
- Enable the primary action when the destination can accept the values on screen. Before calling a form done, type, clear, and change a number, and confirm the button follows.
